  "Main topic of the publication": "This paper explores the evolutionary link between placental invasion and cancer metastasis, proposing that the permissiveness or resistance of uterine stromal cells to placental invasion is mechanistically linked to the vulnerability to cancer malignancy. The study uses comparative transcriptomics and in vitro assays to demonstrate that bovine stroma is more resistant to both trophoblast and melanoma invasion compared to human stroma, suggesting that differences in stromal gene expression contribute to species-specific differences in cancer susceptibility.",
